{"body":{"asks":"Left for the author to weigh after the twenty-second session took the code's binding to components, the address's hidden step and the chassis's link file away: what a card says, written in the language as one function; whether asking, the bar shown or not, a class on the page's body found by selectors, and a list's chosen look are state in the field, buffers, rather than the browser's; a card a component of its own; the holon as the native holon gives it, decoded in one place; the chassis kept apart from its renderer, each concern a file of its own; and links, every card and holon a component draws made an anchor to the page's address by components/web/link.ts, which imports the location's code and names the page's path and param, which the author holds wrong in the twenty-third session: the thread Navigation outside what draws.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M84FFJ1DN05000"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M84FFJ1DN05001","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"The components' remaining glue"}
{"body":{"asks":"A card is just a card: glass at its core is navigation-agnostic, the reader one first example of what navigates, and a URL and a collation are alike, each only where what a reader shows is kept. How does a press on a holon reach whatever navigates? A link naming the page's URL, prop drilling, click bubbling, propose by position and an offer from the root were weighed and let go; a program for navigation is possible, though a side effect.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC000"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Navigation outside what draws"}
{"body":{"asks":"The root reserves gestures and sets the rules of the game, as OpenLight's input floor did; otherwise input is the components'. A gesture, a left or right press or a combination, passes up the holarchy of drawings until captured, the same on any chassis. Is bubbling ever stopped; does a press on a button propagate, or is it deliberately caught; and is a component catching presses and keys itself an antipattern, save input changing only what it was given?","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC001"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Input reserved at the root, propagated until captured"}
{"body":{"asks":"Layers as OpenLight drew them, content and an overlay above it, a kiosk perhaps otherwise, any kind of layer with any implementation; the expression input's completion menu and the context menu its first overlays, kept properly with elevation. The agents leaned completion to the input's own popover instead, which the author holds the absolute opposite of what was drawn, to be grounded further and taken apart.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC002"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Layers and overlays"}
{"body":{"asks":"Right-click is reserved at the root for the context menu, given the place pressed within the holarchy, and the menu component does the expression work from there: pure matching, no scope adding entries, nothing caught and no side effect. Perhaps each level up the tree is a label with its actions, global actions at the bottom, as seeing the layout as nodes. The agents found matching offering too much where most functions take any holon, and the place pressed unknown where a component in code draws a holon in its own markup.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC003"}],"stands":"leaning"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"The context menu as matching over the holarchy"}
{"body":{"asks":"Whatever is mounted in a slot is agnostic and decoupled, and implements no chrome. A component may be its content alone, the parent giving the card and background, which nesting troubles; or the slot gives it. A focus ring and a selection are chrome too, whose shape whatever draws them may not know, and themes differ: perhaps a framework way of splicing into the holarchy. The agents leaned to the host and the look; the author trusts it not yet.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC004"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Chrome around nested components"}
{"body":{"asks":"Chassis of different kinds, DOM and canvas, nested as OpenLight covered; a canvas mounting a visualization as a component taking a particular kind of data; node-based views of holarchies, the interface's own first, offered as a global action. How far OpenLight's ideas are taken is open; the agents asked whether it is one chassis with renderers nested, each answering what stands at a point.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC005"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Chassis of many kinds, nested"}
{"body":{"asks":"Arrow keys and Enter in the completion menu, left and right across cards, / to search the actions at hand rather than the page: all just working, never each component's to implement. Whether the chassis implements it or a piece apart from it, the data to build it probably ships with the field; whether ARIA roles suffice for every layout, a node view among them, or simpler and more powerful data is needed.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M88X8HVYZRC006"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M88X8HVYZRC00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Accessibility and keys defined by the system"}
